{"key":"apphycem-mcq-np1-010","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"Q/(6*epsilon_0)","working":"By Gauss's Law, the total electric flux through the entire closed cubical surface enclosing charge +Q is Phi_total = Q / epsilon_0. Because the point charge is located at the exact center of the cube, the arrangement possesses cubic symmetry, making the electric flux through each of the six identical planar faces equal. Therefore, the flux through any single face is Phi_face = Phi_total / 6 = Q / (6 * epsilon_0).","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":385,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":385,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":372,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":137,"reasoningTokens":235},"totalTokens":757,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":235,"promptTokenCount":385,"candidatesTokenCount":137,"totalTokenCount":757,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":385}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":137}]},"reasoningTokens":235,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3338,"keyed_label":"A"}
